  "findings": [
    "All six original assertions pass in this one observed sample; all11 owner calls and18 actor bodies were observed. No unchanged repeat is needed or selected.",
    "Force fixture installed and entered its existing SIGTERM handler; acknowledged captures preceded actual absolute timeout and SIGKILL.",
    "Progress fixture emitted all seven numbered progress records plus complete; eight parent callbacks acknowledged true; same raw output returned successfully. This sample does not falsify the callback-count criterion.",
    "Unacknowledged fixture had four parent captures returning false; inactivity timeout occurred. A fifth pre-write intent has no write-return marker and is not credited as emitted output.",
    "Post-timeout fixture installed/entered its SIGTERM handler, attempted and completed the111-byte late transcript, then intended exit0. Parent observed the late raw bytes after its timeout callback while semantic finalOutput remained empty.",
    "HTTP-normal published leader, descendant and port metadata; retained full process result status0/no timeout, TERM thenKILL cleanup, confirmed absence. All six grouped modes completed.",
    "Direct-exit leader intended47 and parent observed47 without timeout. Descendant entered and installed225ms timer, but no timer-fire/write attempt was recorded before group termination. Thus this sample supports cleanup; its no-output assertion did not exercise exclusion of actually produced descendant bytes.",
    "Every completed/returned stdout write in the five individual fixtures matches parent raw stdout bytes in this sample; pre-write intent alone is not delivery.",
    "Historical failed actor facts remain erased; no historical startup/load/capture cause is proved by this green diagnostic."
  ],
  "instrumentationLimits": [
    "Fresh relocated compile cache and synchronous fsync sidecars perturb startup/timing; original lease policy/timeouts remain unchanged.",
    "Child local sequence/time is not equated with parent clock. Parent callbacks are observations, not exact timer-arm/signal-delivery times.",
    "For descendant-spawn-return rows the pid field denotes the returned child PID; body-entry pid identifies the emitting process.",
    "Missing marker is not proof of nonexecution; write callback is not proof of parent capture."
  ],
